<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <.legal_page id="terms" title="Terms of Service">
    <section>
      <p>
        These terms apply when you use eventbus. By creating an account you agree to them and to
        the <.link href={~p"/privacy"}>Privacy Policy</.link>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give a real email address you can receive mail at.</li>
        <li>
          Keep your password and your applications' secrets safe. You're responsible for what's
          done with them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Until you confirm your email, your account is limited to a sandbox app with up to 5 topics.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Don't use eventbus to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break the law, or send content that infringes others' rights;</li>
        <li>send spam, malware, or content meant to harass or harm people;</li>
        <li>
          overload the service, probe it for vulnerabilities, or get around its limits or other
          users' access controls.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You're responsible for the events and messages your applications send, and for having
        the right to send them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        eventbus is provided as is, without a service level agreement. Events are delivered
        live and not stored, so an event published while nobody is listening is lost. We may
        change, limit or stop features, and we'll try to give notice for changes that affect
        you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using eventbus at any time. We may suspend or close accounts that break
        these terms or put the service or other users at risk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we're not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or
        for lost data, events or profits, arising from your use of eventbus.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change, the date at the top changes too. Continuing to use eventbus after
        a change means you accept the new terms.
      </p>
    </section>
  </.legal_page>
</Layouts.app>
